/-!
# Constant versus completed integral coefficients

Source: blueprint main-20261015, sec-proetale-coefficients,
`sk-prop-integral-criterion/sk-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients.md`;
Stacks Project, Tags 093M, 099I, 099L, 099M, 099B, 0A0E and 07A6
(blueprint: det-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients).

We use the published coefficient-sized small model of the small pro-etale site.
Only Hom sizes are enlarged. Coefficients and modules live in universe u+1;
ULift is solely the usual change of coefficient universe. Positive level n means n+1.
The completed ring is the actual limit of finite constant ring sheaves, as in the
statement; its pulled-back interpretation is the integral-coefficient-limit theorem.
Completion and its unit are the published universal strict-tower construction.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option synthInstance.maxSize 2048

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.IntegralConstantCompletion

open CategoryTheory.ConstantCompletion

variable (l : ℕ) [Fact l.Prime] (E : Type u) [Field E]
  [Algebra (Padic l) E] [FiniteDimensional (Padic l) E] (X : Scheme.{u})

/-- The existing ring of integers, placed in the module universe.
Source: blueprint constant-coefficients lemma, coefficient notation
(blueprint: det-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients). -/
abbrev integers := ULift.{u + 1} (Padic.coefficientExtensionIntegers l E)

/-- The ideal generated by the specified uniformizer, with no new choice.
Source: blueprint constant-coefficients lemma, pi_E
(blueprint: det-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients). -/
def ideal : Ideal (integers l E) :=
  Ideal.span {ULift.up (Padic.coefficientExtensionUniformizer l E)}

/-- The published equivalent small model of the actual small pro-etale topology.
Source: Stacks 09A5; blueprint constant-coefficients lemma, ambient site
(blueprint: det-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients). -/
abbrev topology := Scheme.coefficientProEtaleModelTopology.{u, u} X

/-- The constant integral coefficient ring R.
Source: blueprint constant-coefficients lemma, R
(blueprint: det-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients). -/
abbrev constantRing := constant (topology X) (integers l E)

/-- The limit B of the positive finite constant coefficient rings.
Source: blueprint constant-coefficients lemma, B; Stacks 099L
(blueprint: det-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients). -/
abbrev completedRing := completed (topology X) (integers l E) (ideal l E)

/-- The canonical completion homomorphism, defined by its quotient cone.
Source: blueprint constant-coefficients lemma, c; Stacks 093M
(blueprint: det-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients). -/
abbrev scalarMap :=
  ConstantCompletion.coefficientMap (topology X) (integers l E) (ideal l E)

/-- The finite coefficient ring R_(n+1), using the given uniformizer ideal.
Source: blueprint constant-coefficients lemma, R_n
(blueprint: det-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients). -/
abbrev finiteRing (n : ℕ) := finite (topology X) (integers l E) (ideal l E) n

/-- The actual quotient map from R (false) or B (true) to the finite coefficient ring.
Source: blueprint constant-coefficients lemma, quotient maps
(blueprint: det-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients). -/
abbrev quotientMap (b : Bool) (n : ℕ) :=
  finiteMap (topology X) (integers l E) (ideal l E) b n

/-- Completeness means invertibility of the specified canonical strict-tower unit.
This is a specialization of the published completion unit, not a new completion model.
Source: blueprint constant-coefficients lemma, definition of completeness; Stacks 099M
(blueprint: det-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients). -/
abbrev Complete (b : Bool) : ObjectProperty
    (D (coefficients (topology X) (integers l E) (ideal l E) b)) :=
  fun M ↦ IsIso ((completionUnit (topology X) (integers l E) (ideal l E) b).app M)

/-- Constant and completed integral coefficients have canonically identical finite
quotients and equivalent derived complete categories. The equivalence is the specified
restriction functor; its inverse is the specified completed derived scalar extension.
The last clause specifies the finite comparison by its pure-tensor formula and its
computation on flat-term K-flat representatives, retaining the finite coefficient action.
The local kernel formula in the first clause means exactly the sheaf quotient by pi^(n+1),
without identifying sheaf quotients with sectionwise quotients.

Source: blueprint main-20261015, constant-coefficients lemma; Stacks 093M, 099I, 099L,
099M, 099B, 0A0E and 07A6
(blueprint: det-prop-integral-criterion-constant-coefficients).

Proof:
1. Set A = O_E and I = (pi_E). The extension-integers DVR theorem makes A a PID,
   hence Noetherian. Pass to the published equivalent small pro-etale site. The identity
   (pi)^m = (pi^m) identifies all finite levels; integral-coefficient-limit identifies
   B with the pulled-back integral sheaf, preserving projections and the scalar map.
   This imposes no Noetherian hypothesis on X or invertibility hypothesis on l.
2. Apply completed-constant-sheaf-reduction (Stacks 093M): B is R-flat and its nth
   quotient projection identifies B/pi^n with R_n. Exact constant-module sheafification
   (constant-module-section-properties, 093J) identifies R/pi^n with R_n. Both maps
   come from the same coefficient quotient, so the induced quotient map is the asserted
   canonical isomorphism. Local surjectivity and the locally principal kernel express
   these quotient identifications on arbitrary test objects.
3. Apply constant-completion-equivalence's finite reduction comparison on a flat-term
   K-flat B-representative. Flatness keeps it K-flat after restriction. The ordinary
   comparison sends s tensor m to s tensor m. Its localization gives the displayed
   natural isomorphism in D(R_n), with the stated computation square.
4. The same general completion equivalence supplies restriction on complete objects.
   Its Koszul/quotient comparison identifies local completeness with invertibility of
   the actual quotient-tower unit, on both R and B, and identifies both units under
   restriction. Thus the full subcategories are precisely those displayed here.
5. Module-pullback-pushforward-adjunction gives scalar extension adjoint to restriction.
   Restriction is exact since it changes no underlying additive sheaf, kernel or cokernel.
   Exact-functor-derived-factorization and exact-functor-derived-functor identify its
   derived functor with termwise restriction. Derived-change-of-rings and
   derived-adjoint-functors give the unbounded derived scalar-extension adjunction.
6. The ringed-Koszul-completion-reflector and the unit-preserving quotient comparison
   make completion on B the reflector onto these complete objects. For complete L,M,
   Hom(C_B(B tensor_R^L L),M) = Hom(B tensor_R^L L,M) = Hom(L,Res M), naturally.
   Uniqueness of the left adjoint to the restriction equivalence identifies its inverse
   with C_B composed with derived scalar extension, giving the second natural isomorphism.
-/
theorem integral_constant_completion :
    SheafOfModules.IsFlatOnSite
      ((res (scalarMap l E X)).obj
        (SheafOfModules.unit (siteModuleRings (completedRing l E X)))) ∧
    (∀ (b : Bool) (n : ℕ),
      Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (topology X) (quotientMap l E X b n).hom ∧
      ∀ (U : Scheme.coefficientProEtaleSiteModel.{u, u} X)
        (x : (coefficients (topology X) (integers l E) (ideal l E) b).obj.obj (op U)),
        (quotientMap l E X b n).hom.app (op U) x = 0 ↔
          ∃ S : Sieve U, S ∈ topology X U ∧
            ∀ (V : Scheme.coefficientProEtaleSiteModel.{u, u} X) (g : V ⟶ U), S g →
              (coefficients (topology X) (integers l E) (ideal l E) b).obj.map g.op x ∈
                Ideal.span
                  {((algebraSection
                    (baseMap (topology X) (integers l E) (ideal l E) b)
                    (ULift.up (Padic.coefficientExtensionUniformizer l E))).val (op V)) ^
                      (n + 1)}) ∧
    (∃ e : (Complete l E X true).FullSubcategory ≌ (Complete l E X false).FullSubcategory,
      Nonempty (e.functor ⋙ (Complete l E X false).ι ≅
        (Complete l E X true).ι ⋙ dres (scalarMap l E X)) ∧
      Nonempty (e.inverse ⋙ (Complete l E X true).ι ≅
        (Complete l E X false).ι ⋙ extend (scalarMap l E X) ⋙
          completion (topology X) (integers l E) (ideal l E) true)) ∧
    ∀ n : ℕ,
      ∃ α : res (scalarMap l E X) ⋙ change (quotientMap l E X false n) ≅
          change (quotientMap l E X true n),
        (∀ (M : Mod (completedRing l E X))
          (U : (Scheme.coefficientProEtaleSiteModel.{u, u} X)ᵒᵖ)
          (s : (finiteRing l E X n).obj.obj U) (m : M.val.obj U),
          (α.hom.app M).val.app U
            (tensorSection (quotientMap l E X false n)
              ((res (scalarMap l E X)).obj M) U s m) =
            tensorSection (quotientMap l E X true n) M U s m) ∧
        ∃ β : extend (quotientMap l E X true n) ≅
            dres (scalarMap l E X) ⋙ extend (quotientMap l E X false n),
          ∀ P : Cx (completedRing l E X), P.IsAcyclicTensorKFlat →
            (∀ q : ℤ, SheafOfModules.IsFlat (P.X q)) →
            (extend (quotientMap l E X false n)).map
                ((resFactors (scalarMap l E X)).inv.app P) ≫
              (extendComparison (quotientMap l E X false n)).app
                (((res (scalarMap l E X)).mapHomologicalComplex (.up ℤ)).obj P) ≫
              (Q (finiteRing l E X n)).map
                ((NatIso.mapHomologicalComplex α (.up ℤ)).hom.app P) =
            β.inv.app ((Q (completedRing l E X)).obj P) ≫
              (extendComparison (quotientMap l E X true n)).app P := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.IntegralConstantCompletion
